{"resourceIdentifier":"340","resourceName":"Upgradation, Operation and Maintenance of 200 TPD Composting facility at Okhla, Delhi","description":"The objective of Okhla MSW Composting Project at Delhi is to avoid methane emissions from anaerobic decomposition of Municipal Solid Waste (MSW) in a landfill site through controlled aerobic decomposition in a windrow composting process. The aerated composting process will avoid methane emissions and will also result in compost as a product that can be utilized as organic fertilizer for agricultural purposes. The Okhla Project treats biodegradable waste predominantly from vegetable market(s) of Delhi and on average it will divert approximately 73,000 tons of MSW per year (200 TPD) that otherwise would be disposed in nearby landfill site if the project was not constructed. With the financial support from carbon credit, this project will demonstrate that the carbon credit finance mechanism can catalyze environmentally sustainable and financially viable waste management practices. Hence the proposed project will provide replicable model for environment friendly and economically viable.","location":{"latitude":28.553525,"longitude":77.281717},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"340"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Delhi"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Indo Enviro Integrated Solutions Private Ltd"},{"type":"string","value":"HARYANA, India"},{"type":"string","value":"+91-124-4297200"},{"type":"string","value":"vishal.sahu@indoenviro.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Late to verify"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"340"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"8525"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type